  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656066",
      "title": "Binding to Custom Properties",
      "lectureOrder": 390,
      "videoOrder": 360,
      "sourceHash": "e0a72510d7e2faa99c9e4a2c78562eaaa314f2e8722cb0e179ae3e2570924cff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "-: So we learned that we can use property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "to bind to our own properties, properties of our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "Now this is what I'll start with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "So to temporarily prevent my app from crashing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "I will simply comment out the code in the cockpit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "so that this doesn't give us any errors anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "For now and we won't be able to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "but it will not crash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "Now in the server component, server element component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "if we have a look at its TypeScript at its HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.55,
          "en": "excuse me, you see that we try to access the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "the single element, the single server element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "and therefore we should create a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 43.38,
          "en": "in this type TypeScript file element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.38,
          "end": 45.57,
          "en": "which represents our server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.57,
          "end": 48.36,
          "en": "We can even assign a type by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.36,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "and then simply defining the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "which will be a JavaScript object, hence to quality braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "And just because it's important, this is not the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 59.97,
          "en": "this is TypeScripts syntax for defining the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 63.9,
          "en": "to make sure that element may only have this type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "And we then know that a element will have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "well, what we're trying to access here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "A type, a name and a content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "So we'll have a type and type on its own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "will be of type string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "we will then have a name which will be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "and will have a content which will be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 85.14,
          "en": "So that is all now our type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.14,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "for a property we want to use in our HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "we use here in all these places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 93.75,
          "en": "Now still this element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.75,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "this property is part of this component only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "of the server element component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "We can't access it from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "Now it would be great if in our app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 107.52000000000001,
          "en": "where we manage our server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "or our array of server elements I should say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 113.07,
          "en": "if we could somehow access this property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.07,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "because let's say just so that we can see something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "we start with one server here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 123.17,
          "en": "which is of type server has a name of TestServer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.17,
          "end": 127.71,
          "en": "and a content of just a test.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.71,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "And just to be super clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "these colons here are not type definitions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 134.67,
          "en": "we're on the right side of the equal sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.67,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "so here we are assigning a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "and the value here simply is a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "and in JavaScript objects we simply assign key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "or we create key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "by having the key then the content and then the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.09,
          "en": "So normal JavaScript syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "So now we got our server elements array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "we're looping through this array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "on the app server element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.57,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "and in the app server element we have our element property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 163.71,
          "en": "So a property in that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.71,
          "end": 167.85,
          "en": "Now we want to access this component from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.85,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "So it would be great if we could bind to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "just like we were able to bind to disabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 176.91,
          "en": "So maybe add squared brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.91,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "enter the name of the property in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 183.94,
          "en": "so the name of the property in the component here, this name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "and then assign the server element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 191.46,
          "en": "So simply the element we store for each iteration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.46,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "in this variable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 195.21,
          "en": "What be great if we could do this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 198.06,
          "en": "And if we try this and our app reloads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.06,
          "end": 202.26,
          "en": "we see that we get an error that we can't bind to element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.26,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "because it isn't a known property of app server element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "Now you might say that is not true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "it is a property of server element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 215.55,
          "en": "here we defined it as a property, it's even public, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.55,
          "end": 217.92000000000002,
          "en": "We didn't add private in front of it or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.92000000000002,
          "end": 219.84300000000002,
          "en": "So why can't we access it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 222.27,
          "en": "Simple answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "Because by default all properties of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "are only accessible inside these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "not from outside and that generally is a good thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 236.91,
          "en": "you don't want to make all your properties bindable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "So you have to be explicit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 243.48,
          "en": "about which properties you want to expose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.48,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "to the world so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 249.63,
          "en": "So if you want to allow parent components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "to be able to bind to this property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "you need to add something to that element property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 258.09,
          "en": "You need to add a decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.09,
          "end": 261.39,
          "en": "Remember, I said that decorators are not only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 261.39,
          "end": 266.22,
          "en": "for classes, here we're going to add one to this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "The decorator we need to add is @Input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 273.48,
          "en": "and here important, you need to execute it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.48,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "it's like a function in the end, so add parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 282.2,
          "en": "and input now needs to be imported from @angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 288.23,
          "en": "With this in place, now we are successfully",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 291.75,
          "en": "exposing this property to the world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.75,
          "end": 293.90999999999997,
          "en": "So now any parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 293.90999999999997,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "any component hosting our server element component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 302.64,
          "en": "so implementing it through its selector like we do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.64,
          "end": 305.64,
          "en": "is now able to bind to element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.64,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "And I can demonstrate this if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "you now see just the test here you see our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "because now we replicate this component for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "well, each element in the array and we successfully can pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 324.98,
          "en": "the element, the property down to that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.74,
          "end": 329.34,
          "en": "and bind to the element property in that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.34,
          "end": 332.76,
          "en": "And this is how you can set up custom property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.76,
          "end": 336.48,
          "en": "on your own events, exposing your own properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 336.48,
          "end": 339.54,
          "en": "to the components where you implement these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.54,
          "end": 341.043,
          "en": "through the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
